CC2D1B (Q5T0F9) is 858 amino acids. MMP20 (O60882) is 386 amino acids. Twice MMP20 = 772 aa, and 858 > 772, so yes.

Note: MMP20 is annotated as a precursor (22 aa signal peptide + 85 aa propeptide, mature chain ~279 aa), so the comparison is even more lopsided when using the mature form; CC2D1B's canonical isoform is 858 aa though alternative isoforms (e.g., isoform 3) are shorter.

